Instruction on how you created the tools isolation for this product.
Please include platform you installed on, where you installed it, what
you copied where, etc.:

Security Directory Integrator v7.2 offers trial versions on Windows x64, Linux x64, and AIX 32 
and uses LUM to implement this.  LUM consists of a platform
independent jar and JNI libraries for each platform.
/*
1.  Download the Common Package
2.  Download Java JNI library for AIX 32, Linux 32 bit xSeries, and Windows 32 bit Intel(Visual C++ 2005 (VC 8) Compiler)
3.  Check LUMClient.jar, libi4trybuyjni.a, libi4trybuyjni.so, and i4trybuyjni.dll into
    CMVC in the adks/ibm/lum/4.6.8.15 directory
*/
1. Copied ibmdi_dev.adks\ibm\lum\4.6.8.15 to ibmdi_dev.adks\ibm\lum\4.6.8.15_64bit
2. Deleted old libi4trybuyjni.so, i4trybuyjni.dll from 4.6.8.15_64bit folder
3. Extracted i4trybuyjni.dll from t_b_for_tdi_tds.zip\lum_4.6.8.15_win_64_msvc8_jni.tar to 4.6.8.15_64bit folder
4. Extracted libi4trybuyjni.so from t_b_for_tdi_tds.zip\lum_4.6.8.15_linux_64_xseries_trybuy_jni.tar to 4.6.8.15_64bit folder
	
	
	
